   "latency_class": "hard_realtime",
   "comment": "Learning progress = the two-timescale surprise-reduction rate (IAC/Oudeyer windowed form; Schmidhuber dC/dt): slow_res - fast_res. POSITIVE when the recent residual is BELOW the older residual (surprise dropping => compressing). ~0 for a RESOLVED item (both EMAs converged) AND for STATIONARY NOISE (both EMAs track the same mean; the noise averages out) -- exactly the noisy-TV discriminator. smoothed_progress mirrors it for the gate/readout.",
   "match": [
    ["hub", "has_curiosity_params", "cp"],
    ["hub", "has_attention_item", "item"]
   ],
   "where": {
    "type": "And",
    "items": [
